## 2. Level architecture (NEW scale — critical)

### Legacy C++ ticket-work (deprecated naming)

The original `cpp-beg-to-adv/ticket-work` used:

| Old folder | Old difficulty |
|------------|----------------|
| `entry-level` | arithmetic, leaks, chaining, const |
| `junior-level` | templates, threads, virtual, concepts |
| `senior-level` | ownership, slicing, friends, ABI |

### New 3-level scale (use from now on)

**The old *senior* difficulty is the new floor (Entry).** Build **up** from there.

| New level | Folder | Ticket ID prefix | Difficulty anchor |
|-----------|--------|------------------|-------------------|
| **Entry** | `entry-level/` | `XXX-ENTRY-1xx` | Same as **former senior**: virtual dtor, slicing, virtual/default-arg traps, `friend`, `operator+` visibility, cross-module ownership |
| **Mid** | `mid-level/` | `XXX-MID-2xx` | Multi-TU linkage, ODR-adjacent mistakes, plugin/DLL boundaries, stress + sanitizer narratives, API contracts across headers |
| **Staff** | `staff-level/` | `XXX-STAFF-3xx` | Certification / security audit tone, intentional UB under load, binary-compat constraints, policy violations spanning 2+ modules |

When generating **new** repos (including **C**):

- Do **not** recreate old entry/junior “easy arithmetic” tiers unless the user explicitly asks for a beginner ticket track.
- Rename mentally: “senior ticket” templates in the reference repo → **Entry ticket** templates in new work.

**Reference mapping (C++ legacy → new):**

| Former senior ticket theme | New Entry ticket |
|---------------------------|------------------|
| VLC-SR-301 virtual ~Codec | ENTRY-101 |
| VLC-SR-302 slicing | ENTRY-102 |
| VLC-SR-303 virtual + default args | ENTRY-103 |
| VLC-SR-304 friend / operator+ | ENTRY-104 |
| VLC-SR-305 factory friend trim | ENTRY-105 |

Mid and Staff tickets are **new designs** at higher scope — not copies of old junior/entry bugs.

