## 8. C course adaptations

When `course-subjects.txt` is for **C** (future `c-beg-to-adv`):

| C++ ticket-work idea | C equivalent |
|---------------------|--------------|
| `virtual` / polymorphism | function pointers in structs, vtable-style manual dispatch |
| `requires` / concepts | prototypes + `_Static_assert` / wrong-type link errors |
| `std::thread` / join | `<pthread.h>` or C11 threads, join before read |
| RAII destructor | explicit `free` / `close` in teardown function |
| `friend` | static file-scope helpers + opaque struct pattern |
| Templates | macros / `_Generic` (C11) where on curriculum |

**Test runner:** same CLI pattern in C (C11 or later).

**Compile-time tests:** prefer `try_compile` CMake tests or separate `.c` snippets — do not break main `ticket_tests.c` when constraint is fixed.

**Naming:** snake_case in C sources; ticket text may use legacy camelCase → document alias in crosswalk.

---

## 9. Language, naming, and engineering tone

- **Professional names:** `UplinkMixer`, `HeapBins`, `AfeRegister` — not `MyStruct`.
- **EE framing:** signal chains, soak tests, HIL, certification, factory trim.
- **Student role:** QA / maintainer fixing regressions, not greenfield feature work.
- **English:** Problem and Fix sections use complete sentences; consistent terminology (observed / expected / PASS / FAIL).

---

## 10. Quality gates before delivery

### Everyday

- [ ] Exercise count == subject count in `course-subjects.txt`
- [ ] Order matches file exactly
- [ ] Every exercise has reveal button with solution + why
- [ ] No solution in visible task text

### Ticket-work

- [ ] 15 tickets, 5 per level, IDs stable
- [ ] Every ticket: Problem / Fix / Reproduce / Pass / Hint / Solution panels
- [ ] **Fix sections contain no solution language** (§5.2)
- [ ] Bug baseline: all tests compile; all FAIL
- [ ] Test stdout: observed + expected + PASS/FAIL only
- [ ] Compile-time tickets: tests compile after fix (§4.5)
- [ ] `TICKET_CROSSWALK.md` complete
- [ ] `README.md` has build + single-ticket test commands

